Z||000024||AusFiero||06-18-2001||12:12 AM||||How about keeping the stock headlight flaps and mechanisms. Make them pop up part of the height they do now and instead of having large squarish lights fit 2 small round headlights. Very small ones to make the flaps hardly have to be up much at all.<P>Would tie in well with your rear fascia.<P>Maybe mount the low beam one slightly further forward in the new buckets for effect.<P>To tie in with the look I will have driving light indicators available soon. Put them in the stock indicator locations and they will have an orange globe as an indicator, or turn on the other globes for the main 150 W driving lights. Will also have shaped driving and or fog lights available that fit snuggly into the edges of the front GT Fasica, edges of the radiator intake hole that is.<P>Suggestion and shameless plug all in one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Should I just make the headlight kit too and be done with? <P>Would probably cost around US$200 to $250 shipped. Including all fittings of course to just bolt it all in. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000025||AusFiero||06-18-2001||12:18 AM||||Or alternatively I can get you some really nicely shaped headlights for good prices. Have 1 type in mind that would work in the front fascia real well actually. Is hard to explain the shape but kinda like 2 ovals overlapping and joined together as a single unit. They are tiny but effective, 120 watt high beams and 55 watt low beams.<BR>Will post some pics on Thursday night after I spend a day taking photos of all the new toys and goodies I have found that are feasible to sell and ship to America for good prices.||||reg||1
